(b) the point of an outage (in terruption);
(c) the time at which the service is restored, allowing for staged restoration of a major interruption;
(d) total duration of interruption for each restoration stage;
(e) affected feeder and transformer code number;
(f) tiie number of connected consumers; and
(g) the number of consumers affected by each interruption.
